# Getting started skill

A skill is authored **once, as docs**. This `app` composition names the subset of
documentation pages that an onboarding skill needs, and `work weave` assembles them
into a `SKILL.md` next to this file — frontmatter plus each page's `.work` source
verbatim. We never hand-edit the generated skill; we edit the docs it composes.

The convention is the same `app` / `section` / `page` used by the docs index — the
only difference is location: an `app` under `skills/` assembles to markdown, the
index `app` assembles to the HTML site.

app :getting_started do
  title       "Getting started with Workbooks"
  description "Author and ship .work workbooks. Use when starting a new workbook, learning the .work format, or onboarding a CLI agent to the work CLI."

  section "What it is" do
    page "introduction/what-is-a-workbook"
    page "introduction/what-is-a-work-file"
  end

  section "The work CLI" do
    page "introduction/what-is-the-work-cli"
    page "tooling/get-started-with-your-cli-agent"
  end
end
